<title>AUSTRIA: Creditanstalt 6-mo oper profit up 38 pct.</title>
<headline>Creditanstalt 6-mo oper profit up 38 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>First six months of the year to June 30, 1997. (Figures in billions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>							1997	 1996</p>
<p> Group operating income			10.855	9.078</p>
<p> Group operating expenses		     6.649	6.037</p>
<p> Group operating result			 4.206	3.041</p>
<p>NOTES - Creditanstalt holds a news conference on its first half earnings at 0800 GMT.</p>
<p>According to Austrian accounting standards, operating profit is calculated before risk provisions.</p>
<p>Creditanstalt is majority controlled by Bank Austria, which in January acquired two-thirds of the bank's voting shares from the Republic of Austria for 17.2 billion schillings. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
